      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, you should not suddenly eat large amounts of spinach and kale while on warfarin because leafy greens contain Vitamin K, which can interact with the medication. Sudden changes in Vitamin K intake might cause your INR to drop too low, increasing your risk of potential clots. Instead, try to keep your Vitamin K intake consistent and consult your doctor before making specific dietary adjustments. They may need to adjust your warfarin dosage once they see your lab results reflecting your new diet. Always follow your doctor's guidance to maintain the safe balance between heart health and blood thinning medication.",
